(CHAPTER 1: INFORMED SEARCH & ADVERSARIAL ALGORITHMS \(Page 1\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Search & Logic · Section 1.1 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Search algorithms navigate state spaces from an initial state to a goal state.) Tj T*
(Uninformed search strategies \(BFS, DFS\) explore without domain knowledge. BFS expands) Tj T*
(the shallowest node using a FIFO queue, guaranteeing completeness and optimality for) Tj T*
(unit-cost step problems, with time and space complexity O\(b^d\). DFS expands the) Tj T*
(deepest unexpanded node using a LIFO stack, with space complexity O\(b*m\), but is not) Tj T*
(optimal and can trap in infinite loops without cycle detection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Search & Logic · Section 1.2 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Informed \(Heuristic\) search leverages a heuristic function h\(n\) estimating the) Tj T*
(cheapest path from node n to the goal.) Tj T*
(The A* search algorithm evaluates nodes using f\(n\) = g\(n\) + h\(n\), where g\(n\) is the) Tj T*
(exact cost incurred from the start node to n, and h\(n\) is the estimated cost from n to) Tj T*
(the goal.) Tj T*
(A heuristic h\(n\) is admissible if it never overestimates the true cost to reach the) Tj T*
(goal: 0 <= h\(n\) <= h*\(n\).) Tj T*
(A heuristic is consistent \(monotonic\) if for every node n and successor n' generated) Tj T*
(by action a: h\(n\) <= c\(n, a, n'\) + h\(n'\) and h\(Goal\) = 0.) Tj T*
(Theorem: If h\(n\) is admissible on tree search, or consistent on graph search, A* is) Tj T*
(guaranteed to be complete and optimal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Search & Logic · Section 1.3 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(In two-player zero-sum games, the Minimax algorithm computes optimal decisions) Tj T*
(assuming an adversarial opponent.) Tj T*
(Alpha-Beta pruning eliminates subtrees that cannot influence the final decision) Tj T*
(without losing optimality:) Tj T*
(- Alpha \(alpha\): The highest-value choice found so far along any choice point for MAX.) Tj T*
(Initialized to -infinity.) Tj T*
(- Beta \(beta\): The lowest-value choice found so far along any choice point for MIN.) Tj T*
(Initialized to +infinity.) Tj T*
(A branch is pruned whenever alpha >= beta. In the ideal move-ordering case, alpha-beta) Tj T*
(pruning reduces the effective branching factor from b to sqrt\(b\), doubling the) Tj T*
(reachable search depth.) Tj T*
ET
