(CHAPTER 3: ATTENTION & TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES \(Page 3\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: Transformers · Section 3.1 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(The Transformer architecture \(Vaswani et al., 2017\) dispenses with recurrent) Tj T*
(recurrences entirely, computing token dependencies in parallel via Self-Attention.) Tj T*
(Given an input sequence mapped to embedding matrix X in R^\(n x d_model\), linear) Tj T*
(projections yield Queries \(Q = X * W_Q\), Keys \(K = X * W_K\), and Values \(V = X * W_V\),) Tj T*
(where W_Q, W_K in R^\(d_model x d_k\) and W_V in R^\(d_model x d_v\).) Tj T*
(Scaled Dot-Product Attention is formulated as:) Tj T*
(Attention\(Q, K, V\) = softmax\(\(Q * K^T\) / sqrt\(d_k\)\) * V) Tj T*
(The scaling factor 1 / sqrt\(d_k\) prevents the dot products from growing excessively) Tj T*
(large for high dimensions d_k, which would push the softmax function into regions with) Tj T*
(near-zero gradients.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: Transformers · Section 3.2 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(Multi-Head Attention \(MHA\) projects queries, keys, and values h times into different) Tj T*
(representation subspaces:) Tj T*
(MultiHead\(Q, K, V\) = Concat\(head_1, ..., head_h\) * W_O) Tj T*
(where head_i = Attention\(Q * W_Q^\(i\), K * W_K^\(i\), V * W_V^\(i\)\). This allows the model) Tj T*
(to simultaneously attend to information from different representation subspaces at) Tj T*
(different positions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: Transformers · Section 3.3 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(In decoder-only autoregressive LLMs \(like GPT and LLaMA\), causal masking is applied to) Tj T*
(ensure prediction of token at position t depends only on tokens at indices <= t.) Tj T*
(During inference, recomputing all key and value tensors for prior tokens at every) Tj T*
(generation step scales quadratically O\(t^2\). The KV-Cache retains key and value) Tj T*
(projections for past tokens in GPU memory, reducing step generation complexity to) Tj T*
(O\(t\). Rotary Position Embeddings \(RoPE\) encode relative token distances by rotating) Tj T*
(the query and key vectors in complex 2D planes, preserving relative distance decay) Tj T*
(across long context windows.) Tj T*
ET
